WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
16 years and 8 months is the sentence for the surrey bus attack. This is vancouver daily, episode 38. I'm

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:13.380
Mira, the Nerranetwork's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After that, a new fire chief for vancouver,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.280
a second murder verdict on a Fraser Street shooting, and richmond's move to take its wave pool,

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:25.520
then the roads and the canucks. Abdul Aziz-Kawam is the man CBC says was convicted in 2025 for the

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.700
Islamic State knife attack on a BC bus.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.880
The sentence splits into 15 years for attempted murder and 20 months for aggravated assault.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.880
Global News says security video from April 1, 2023 shows him walking onto the bus with

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.340
his victim a few seconds behind.

00:00:41.505 --> 00:00:45.945
Robert Weeks is the longtime deputy the Vancouver Sun says will lead Vancouver Fire Rescue

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:46.345
Services.

00:00:46.825 --> 00:00:50.185
He starts Monday, November 2, after a country-wide search.

00:00:50.525 --> 00:00:52.745
That is the top job at the city's fire service.

00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:58.345
Alvaro Julio Rochegarcia is the man a global BC jury has now found guilty of first-degree

00:00:58.345 --> 00:00:59.625
murder for a second time.

00:01:00.105 --> 00:01:05.905
The victim is Zenon Zapata Silva, 69, shot in January 2019 while he sat with his wife

00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:07.305
on a porch on Fraser Street.

00:01:07.965 --> 00:01:10.265
Rochegarcia was arrested shortly after that shooting.

00:01:10.865 --> 00:01:14.185
Silva's wife had a stroke before the first trial and never testified there.

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:18.825
That jury heard a preliminary inquiry recording in which she said his dying words were that

00:01:18.825 --> 00:01:19.985
Alvaro had killed him.

00:01:19.985 --> 00:01:24.365
The province's highest court said the judge was wrong to let the jury treat that statement

00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:26.145
as fact without cross-examination.

00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:29.885
Struck the conviction in 2024 and ordered a new trial.

00:01:30.385 --> 00:01:32.705
Five weeks later, the new jury convicted him again.

00:01:33.165 --> 00:01:35.245
Global says no motive was ever made clear.

00:01:35.745 --> 00:01:39.845
Crown counsel Daniel Port said the couple had known him about 15 years in Albuquerque

00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:40.405
in Vancouver.

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.865
He told the court he had no reason to shoot.

00:01:43.305 --> 00:01:47.405
His lawyer argued the hard evidence was missing, and sentencing is set for next month.

00:01:47.405 --> 00:01:54.873
Surrey Schools has put out an updated accessibility plan for 2026 through 2028, Education News Canada

00:01:54.873 --> 00:01:59.653
reports, after finishing the first three years of the plan that began in September 2023.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:04.513
That first plan followed the accessible British Columbia regulation, which from September

00:02:04.513 --> 00:02:10.053
2023 required public bodies to have accessibility committees, plans, and a way for the public

00:02:10.053 --> 00:02:10.793
to give feedback.

00:02:11.313 --> 00:02:15.993
Superintendent Shawna Ross and district principal Colin Reed presented the update at the

00:02:15.993 --> 00:02:17.013
October Board Meeting.

00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:20.293
Read said a district-wide look at parking lots, entrances,

00:02:20.753 --> 00:02:23.393
doors, learning commons, and emergency preparedness

00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:25.833
is already shaping renovations and new buildings.

00:02:26.353 --> 00:02:29.253
He said an animated video series on accessibility language

00:02:29.253 --> 00:02:30.853
has been viewed thousands of times

00:02:30.853 --> 00:02:34.473
and picked up by municipalities, nonprofits, advocacy

00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:36.233
groups, and other BC districts.

00:02:36.773 --> 00:02:38.833
Next, the district wants yearly site checks

00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:41.193
and accessibility page on each school site,

00:02:41.633 --> 00:02:44.233
National Accessibility Week built with student input

00:02:44.233 --> 00:02:51.013
and tactile wayfinding at DEC, REC, and Sunnyside Elementary, and Reed said the work has held to the line

00:02:51.013 --> 00:02:57.377
nothing about us without us. Ellen Peterson teaches kindergarten at Ray Shepard Elementary in South Surrey,

00:02:57.617 --> 00:03:01.997
and Education News Canada says she has won the Susan Langley Earth Steward Teaching Award

00:03:01.997 --> 00:03:07.077
from learning for a sustainable future. For six years her class has spent part of every school day

00:03:07.077 --> 00:03:11.317
in the forest beside the school, whatever the weather. They do math with pine cones,

00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:15.437
art with leaves and science by watching insects, weather, and the seasons.

00:03:16.017 --> 00:03:20.817
Peterson says five-year-olds may not grasp climate change or biodiversity loss the way adults do,

00:03:21.157 --> 00:03:25.177
but they do understand wonder, curiosity, and care for a place they love.

00:03:25.737 --> 00:03:29.777
In 2020, a senior the class calls Grand Friend Dawn started coming out with them,

00:03:30.217 --> 00:03:33.577
and grandparents, retirees, parents, and other elders followed.

00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:38.257
She teaches reciprocity, bird feeders in winter, bug hotels in the fall,

00:03:38.257 --> 00:03:42.377
space is kept clean and she said children need to love the earth before anyone

00:03:42.377 --> 00:03:46.965
asks them to save it. Richmond is trying to take ownership of Water Mania by

00:03:46.965 --> 00:03:52.085
expropriation before the lease runs out in March 2027. Daily Hive says the city's

00:03:52.085 --> 00:03:57.645
notice is dated July 3rd, 2026 and was filed with the land title office on July 6th.

00:03:57.945 --> 00:04:02.065
The registered owner named on that notice is 14300 entertainment boulevard

00:04:02.065 --> 00:04:06.745
investments. The pool is at the Riverport Complex in Southeast Richmond next to

00:04:06.745 --> 00:04:10.785
the cinema, the bowling alley, and the ice center. The city runs it as a public

00:04:10.785 --> 00:04:14.865
rec center but has never owned the building or the land. Both have been leased

00:04:14.865 --> 00:04:18.785
from a private owner since the place opened nearly 30 years ago. The notice

00:04:18.785 --> 00:04:22.805
says a takeover would keep an indoor aquatic center and fitness facility as an

00:04:22.805 --> 00:04:26.765
essential community service and would let the city manage the asset by owning the

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:30.865
land outright. Those services could be run by Richmond itself or by another

00:04:30.865 --> 00:04:34.925
public body acting for the city. The private owner has started an independent

00:04:34.925 --> 00:04:41.625
inquiry set to begin in late November 2026. Outgoing mayor Malcolm Brody told Daily Hive the city almost

00:04:41.625 --> 00:04:47.325
never expropriates and avoids it when it can, that water mania matters to the community and that the

00:04:47.325 --> 00:04:52.085
goal is to lock in its future. He said he would not comment further while the inquiry is underway

00:04:52.085 --> 00:04:57.945
and that the city wants a fair outcome. Voters approved borrowing about $20 million in a 1993

00:04:57.945 --> 00:05:03.605
referendum for a city-owned pool on city land. Council then dropped that plan to avoid more debt

00:05:03.605 --> 00:05:07.605
and took the Riverport developers offer to finance the building and lease it back.

00:05:08.085 --> 00:05:09.965
Watermania opened in 1997.

00:05:10.445 --> 00:05:17.505
The latest BC assessment role puts the property at $49.4 million, $27.41 million for the land,

00:05:17.745 --> 00:05:22.185
and $21.99 million for the building, as of July 1st, 2025.

00:05:22.905 --> 00:05:28.085
In 2019, the city bought the neighboring ice center, which had the same private build, city lease setup,

00:05:28.385 --> 00:05:30.905
and said the old lease payments would help pay for upgrades.

00:05:31.405 --> 00:05:32.725
The Olympic oval was different.

00:05:32.725 --> 00:05:36.385
The city owned it from the start, built for speed skating in 2010.

00:05:37.025 --> 00:05:41.745
Richmond's four public swim sites are Watermania and Menoru for year-round indoor swimming,

00:05:42.025 --> 00:05:44.985
plus seasonal outdoor pools at South Arm and Steveston.

00:05:45.525 --> 00:05:51.025
What is on the line for users is the Wave Pool, two long slides and a 57 meter competition pool

00:05:51.025 --> 00:05:56.165
with a movable bulkhead, along with the fitness center, springboards, a five meter tower,

00:05:56.645 --> 00:05:58.645
whirlpools, a steam room, and a sauna.

00:05:58.645 --> 00:06:02.685
Brody's case is that owning the site is how the city keeps that public use.

00:06:03.145 --> 00:06:06.245
The owner's step, as reported, is that late November inquiry.

00:06:06.725 --> 00:06:09.585
A separate cloud on the value comes from August 2025,

00:06:09.585 --> 00:06:13.545
when Justice Barbara Young granted the Cowachan Tribes Aboriginal title

00:06:13.545 --> 00:06:17.085
over about 740 acres north and east of Riverport.

00:06:17.705 --> 00:06:22.165
Richmond, Ottawa, the province, Musqueam, and Sowasin have all appealed.

00:06:22.565 --> 00:06:27.965
The Cowachan Tribes have appealed too, seeking title over the full 1,846 acres

00:06:27.965 --> 00:06:32.285
of the original claim. And a city map shows that wider area includes riverport.

00:06:32.905 --> 00:06:37.085
Daily Hive says those appeals could take many years, and that it is still unclear what the

00:06:37.085 --> 00:06:42.405
ruling does to this property's assessment. Also today, the Squamish Nation will honor a humpback

